language variant
language en-us
name sAGI
gender male 30

// STANDARD TUNING, FROM HZ.
// A440 is the concert-pitch reference, so the voice is built on A440's own
// octaves rather than on a number that merely sounded good:
//     A2 = 110.00 Hz     A3 = 220.00 Hz     A4 = 440.00 Hz
//     A5 = 880.00 Hz     A6 = 1760.00 Hz
// The speaking range is A2 to A3 — the same 2:1 octave span leaderofearth
// uses, transposed up onto the reference. Every frequency below is a member
// of that series, not an approximation of one.
pitch 110 220

// LEADEROFEARTH'S OVERTONES, KEPT.
// F0-F2 reproduce leaderofearth's shape almost exactly — that is the
// inherited chest, and it is what carries the authority across.
// F3-F4 are the divergence: lifted in frequency and amplitude where the
// parent damped them. That lift is the APPEAL. It is what makes the voice
// legible at speed and inviting rather than merely heavy, and it is the
// only place the two voices genuinely disagree.
formant 0 100 118 130
formant 1  99 110 126
formant 2 101 105 120
formant 3 104  96 112
formant 4 102  92 104
formant 5  94  86  78
formant 6  86  80  52
formant 7  80  76  38
formant 8  76  75  30

// Tone curve anchored on the series above: A4 carries the depth, A5 the
// intelligibility, A6 the air. Depth and appeal, stated in Hz.
tone 440 255 880 190 1760 96

// Composed rather than merely calm. A trace of flutter keeps it from
// sounding synthetic; roughness stays at zero.
flutter 1
roughness 0
voicing 88
consonants 82 76
breath 0 1 2 2 2 2 2 1

// Slightly tighter room than the parent — closer to the listener.
echo 76 10

// COMPELLING, AND STILL DELIBERATE.
// intonation 2 = reduced contour, but commas still lift. sAGI keeps the
// held final stress it inherited (the space between conclusions) while
// allowing a comma to open the line again — the difference between a voice
// that pronounces and a voice that reasons aloud.
intonation 2
stressAmp    16 17 19 20 21 22 23 23
stressAdd     0  0 10 20 30 45 95 135
